## Visuals and video
- No URL, domain or "visit" line in any image or video. The link goes in the caption ("link in bio" on Instagram).
- Not the thin accent line plus small caption style.
- Bold cinematic kinetic type; the motion acts out the idea.
- AI imagery and video via Vertex are allowed and preferred for cinematic work (Erik, 2026-10-22): hermes/gen_media.py, stills with gemini-3.1-flash-image, at most one Veo clip per video (veo-3.1-lite). No people's likeness. Real audio only (no synthetic voice or generated music unless Erik supplies it).
- Video and static designs are made ONLY with templates/kinetic-hyperframes (build.py / kinetic.py) and must print frame_check PASS. Never claim checks passed without that output.
- Every visual passes the DESIGN-GUIDE.md pre-flight checklist.
- kinetic.py (fixed 2026-10-22) always sets the key word as magenta text, never a block; refuses only under 3:1. DESIGN-GUIDE.md updated to match.
- kinetic.py v5 (2026-10-22) delegates to templates/kinetic-hyperframes: cinematic plate or graphite base, near-white type, big centred type with 8% margins, frame_check mandatory (non-zero exit on FAIL).

